# .intentfiles -- WHICH DATABASE ARTEFACTS ALSO HAVE A REALISED FORM ON DISK.
#
# Written on hv's order 2026-08-26 from thread status (organize --default was not yet
# built): every OPEN thread is declared, and nothing else. OPEN means every status
# except Completed and Cancelled.
#
# HOW TO CHANGE IT, which the line above does not say. `intent st hydrate <ID>` adds a
# thread here and writes its files; `intent st dehydrate <ID>` is the inverse. Reach for
# those rather than editing this file by hand: the file and the tree are reconciled by
# `intent organize`, so a hand-edit the tree does not match is removed on the next
# `--apply`.
#
# AND THE RULE ABOVE IS NOT THE RULE THE TOOL IMPLEMENTS, though the two agree today.
# `organize --default` writes one STEELTHREAD line per WIP thread; the header's rule is
# every OPEN thread, which also admits Not Started. ST0017 is currently the only
# non-Completed thread and it is WIP, so both rules produce this exact file -- a Not
# Started thread is what would separate them. Measured 2026-09-09, amended on hv's
# ruling the same day; the provenance above is kept rather than regenerated away.
#
STEELTHREAD:ST0017
